      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s five wooden grain elevators, once called “Elevator Row,” were demolished in the 1970s, leaving only one converted into an art gallery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawson_Creek",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During World War II, Dawson Creek hosted a Royal Canadian Air Force station that opened in September 1944 and operated until 1964.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawson_Creek",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since 1959, CJDC‑TV has broadcast from Dawson Creek, shifting from a CBC affiliate to a CTV 2 affiliation in 2016.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
